WEBVTT

00:00:05.535 --> 00:00:10.101
Candy went for a vacation to
a Summer school in Scotland,

00:00:10.456 --> 00:00:13.600
...where she happened upon Terry's real mother.

00:00:17.725 --> 00:00:27.822
Terry, however, kept insisting that the woman who came
from America to see him, isn't his real mother.

00:00:30.042 --> 00:00:36.542
The link between a mother and a child.

00:00:48.212 --> 00:00:51.058
Kurin, it's still too early to get up.

00:00:56.547 --> 00:01:00.174
I see... you want us to play
before everybody gets up?

00:01:12.402 --> 00:01:13.662
Wait up, Kurin!

00:01:19.415 --> 00:01:20.955
You're tickling me! Stop that, Kurin!

00:01:21.715 --> 00:01:23.171
Kurin, you!

00:01:25.056 --> 00:01:26.260
Got you!

00:01:26.749 --> 00:01:30.265
Kurin, it's been a long time since
the two of us played like this!

00:01:32.668 --> 00:01:37.376
It's because you always have to hide
so that people don't see you.

00:01:39.590 --> 00:01:43.021
From now on, I'll get up earlier
so I can play with you.

00:01:43.405 --> 00:01:44.946
Now, let's run!

00:01:56.370 --> 00:01:57.807
Wonderful!

00:02:07.279 --> 00:02:08.387
Alright!

00:02:08.739 --> 00:02:10.672
I haven't climbed a tree in a long time, too!

00:02:16.281 --> 00:02:17.760
I'm not gonna give up!

00:02:28.262 --> 00:02:31.059
I haven't felt this good for a long time, Kurin!

00:02:33.945 --> 00:02:34.805
Beautiful!

00:02:35.293 --> 00:02:37.283
Terry's mansion is over there.

00:02:39.166 --> 00:02:40.565
Eleanor Baker?

00:02:40.908 --> 00:02:42.546
It's Terry's mother.

00:02:50.193 --> 00:02:53.387
Terry, please, open the gates.

00:02:53.575 --> 00:02:54.617
Go back.

00:02:54.703 --> 00:02:58.011
I already told you last night
that I never want to see you again.

00:02:58.104 --> 00:03:00.620
Please... hear my story for the last time!

00:03:00.728 --> 00:03:04.041
If you keep yelling here, somebody
is going to come. Got it?

00:03:05.146 --> 00:03:09.901
It would be a disgrace if people found out
that an upstanding American actress has such a son!

00:03:10.064 --> 00:03:13.829
Terry, I'll be returning to America
this evening.

00:03:18.918 --> 00:03:22.530
That look on Terry face... it's the same
look he had on the day we first met.

00:03:26.187 --> 00:03:28.713
Frightened... sad...

00:03:30.465 --> 00:03:31.911
I have nothing else to say to you.

00:03:32.479 --> 00:03:33.956
Terry, please wait!

00:03:34.535 --> 00:03:35.659
Don't go!

00:03:36.826 --> 00:03:38.340
Terry.

00:03:42.220 --> 00:03:43.632
Terry.

00:03:48.913 --> 00:03:50.012
Uh...

00:03:53.940 --> 00:03:56.093
Oh, no! The breakfast!

00:04:02.486 --> 00:04:04.188
Kurin, let's take a shortcut!

00:04:17.962 --> 00:04:19.606
Romeo and Juliet.

00:04:19.948 --> 00:04:21.324
A scenario book.

00:04:26.354 --> 00:04:28.912
E.B.
Eleanor Baker.

00:04:29.549 --> 00:04:31.505
This book belongs to Terry's mother.

00:04:31.685 --> 00:04:34.067
I'll return it to her
during my free time in the afternoon.

00:04:39.861 --> 00:04:42.190
You're the only one who hasn't shown
up for the breakfast!

00:04:42.717 --> 00:04:44.938
You haven't told anybody about your leave...

00:04:45.100 --> 00:04:46.391
Where were you going this early in the morning?

00:04:46.578 --> 00:04:49.622
Uh... for a walk...

00:04:50.341 --> 00:04:54.170
I see. In that case, you'll spend
the free time in your room.

00:04:54.358 --> 00:04:56.191
But... I don't want that...

00:04:57.699 --> 00:04:59.921
I won't be able to return this book.

00:05:02.012 --> 00:05:03.972
Good morning, sister!

00:05:04.356 --> 00:05:07.956
-Candy, thanks for your help!
-Mark.

00:05:08.740 --> 00:05:16.295
-Sister, Candice came to help us with milking.
-We got this much.

00:05:16.818 --> 00:05:18.686
Candice helped out with milking?

00:05:19.024 --> 00:05:22.000
She was a great help to us!

00:05:22.177 --> 00:05:25.852
Why haven't you honestly
told me about this, Candice?

00:05:26.197 --> 00:05:27.581
Yes...

00:05:27.940 --> 00:05:32.407
In that case, I'll allow you out
due to the circumstances.

00:05:33.137 --> 00:05:34.808
Thank you!

00:05:38.754 --> 00:05:41.424
-Lady! Mark!
-Hello!

00:05:43.883 --> 00:05:47.172
-You just saved me.
-It's okay!

00:05:48.870 --> 00:05:51.181
Even lies are sometimes useful.

00:05:52.111 --> 00:05:56.525
Oh! Both you and Mark winked your left eyes!

00:05:57.054 --> 00:05:58.333
Come to think of it...

00:05:59.631 --> 00:06:01.018
I never realized!

00:06:02.097 --> 00:06:05.409
Parents and their kids see things the same way...

00:06:06.029 --> 00:06:08.113
-Let's go, mom!
-Okay.

00:06:08.385 --> 00:06:09.607
Well then, miss!

00:06:12.903 --> 00:06:15.419
-See you!
-Goodbye!

00:06:23.742 --> 00:06:27.080
Is there a way to make Terry and his mother
get along like those two?

00:06:27.106 --> 00:06:28.682
They're family!

00:06:36.788 --> 00:06:40.227
This is probably it. The hotel where
Terry's mother is staying.

00:06:41.538 --> 00:06:44.031
-What a pity, bro.
-Maybe we'll get another chance.

00:06:44.032 --> 00:06:45.200
Stear!

00:06:45.877 --> 00:06:47.012
Hi, Candy!

00:06:47.313 --> 00:06:49.340
Do you have any business in this hotel?

00:06:49.515 --> 00:06:51.200
Yeah... a little.

00:06:51.769 --> 00:06:53.609
What are you two here for?

00:06:53.973 --> 00:06:55.355
Tell her, bro!

00:06:56.149 --> 00:06:57.351
Anyway, it's...

00:06:57.506 --> 00:07:00.089
Be a man, say it out loud!

00:07:00.552 --> 00:07:05.452
-Bro, you're in charge of things like these!
-But you're better in this than me...

00:07:06.002 --> 00:07:08.630
Anyway, we came here to get an autograph.

00:07:09.174 --> 00:07:09.894
An autograph?

00:07:09.929 --> 00:07:14.923
We heard rumours that Eleanor Baker is
staying at this hotel.

00:07:14.975 --> 00:07:17.308
Then... did you get her autograph?

00:07:18.044 --> 00:07:21.801
We barely missed her. Looks like she
already departed to America.

00:07:22.790 --> 00:07:24.404
To America?

00:07:24.971 --> 00:07:27.689
By the way, what did you come here for?

00:07:28.967 --> 00:07:30.977
It doesn't matter anymore.

00:07:31.740 --> 00:07:32.911
Hey, Candy...

00:07:42.503 --> 00:07:46.317
I can't change Terry's stubbornness anymore...

00:07:50.621 --> 00:07:51.787
What about me?

00:07:52.733 --> 00:07:53.773
Terry!

00:07:53.934 --> 00:07:58.115
I'm happy to see you calling out my name
alone like this...

00:07:58.347 --> 00:08:00.442
He looks completely different
from what I saw this morning.

00:08:00.479 --> 00:08:02.562
Maybe he spoke to his mother, after all?

00:08:02.972 --> 00:08:08.834
Say, I had no idea that I'm on your mind
at times when you're alone.

00:08:09.405 --> 00:08:10.544
Don't talk such nonsense!

00:08:11.683 --> 00:08:14.083
You always reinforce your words with fists!

00:08:14.660 --> 00:08:17.180
Candy, that book...

00:08:19.107 --> 00:08:20.574
To whom do you think it belongs?

00:08:21.111 --> 00:08:23.948
To whom... maybe...

00:08:24.325 --> 00:08:24.984
Here!

00:08:25.970 --> 00:08:28.108
-It's my book!
-Your book?

00:08:28.337 --> 00:08:32.371
Terry, you read scenarios?
I'm surprised! How come?

00:08:32.605 --> 00:08:33.648
Say, Candy...

00:08:34.207 --> 00:08:36.848
Even if you turn into a wrinkled old granny,
you'd still be Candy, right?

00:08:37.471 --> 00:08:39.043
Don't say such weird things!

00:08:39.445 --> 00:08:43.152
And even if I become a gray old gentleman,
I'd still be Terry, right?

00:08:43.252 --> 00:08:45.485
Hm! You were the only one
who looked cool now!

00:08:46.015 --> 00:08:49.428
Then, are you saying that
we can't turn into other people?

00:08:50.574 --> 00:08:52.519
But the thing is - acting is different.

00:09:17.992 --> 00:09:21.166
You can become someone else on the stage.
Even a king.

00:09:28.621 --> 00:09:30.535
You can even kill someone.

00:09:48.514 --> 00:09:49.940
And... you can love, too.

00:09:53.175 --> 00:09:54.167
Terry!

00:09:57.029 --> 00:10:01.227
I was just kidding!
My partner would have to be much cuter.

00:10:01.832 --> 00:10:03.258
Some things you say!

00:10:04.122 --> 00:10:09.613
There is a small world on the stage.
A wonderful world, overflowing with dreams.

00:10:10.162 --> 00:10:14.893
Terry's face lit up. I've never seen
such a vigor in his eyes.

00:10:15.475 --> 00:10:18.457
But I've already seen a person
with such an expression!

00:10:19.807 --> 00:10:21.106
Anthony?

00:10:21.202 --> 00:10:23.831
It was Anthony, at times when he
was tending his roses.

00:10:25.014 --> 00:10:26.104
Anthony.

00:10:28.633 --> 00:10:29.804
Said something?

00:10:30.977 --> 00:10:33.165
Nah, it's nothing.

00:10:38.797 --> 00:10:41.542
*Demented Anime Fansub*
This episode reeks of longplay VHS. I'm so sorry for that.
You have no idea how sorry I am.

00:10:49.365 --> 00:10:52.042
Say, wanna stop by?
I'll put the kettle on.

00:10:52.597 --> 00:10:55.394
Terry, you'll make tea?
Can you manage?

00:10:55.532 --> 00:10:56.611
When you put it this way...

00:11:02.003 --> 00:11:02.979
Terry!

00:11:07.844 --> 00:11:09.787
You're still loitering around?

00:11:09.986 --> 00:11:14.592
I wanted to speak to you one last time
before returning to America.

00:11:14.773 --> 00:11:15.549
Go back.

00:11:16.231 --> 00:11:17.452
I don't want to speak to you.

00:11:17.819 --> 00:11:18.897
Terry...!

00:11:22.911 --> 00:11:26.083
Somebody is coming. Terry, you'd
better open the gates.

00:11:32.054 --> 00:11:35.614
Terry, I'm begging you...
please hear my story!

00:11:36.649 --> 00:11:37.369
Shut up!

00:11:37.652 --> 00:11:40.729
After what you said back then - -
I don't have a mother anymore!

00:11:40.802 --> 00:11:42.884
Please understand, Terrius!

00:11:43.722 --> 00:11:45.634
There was nothing I could do back then.

00:11:47.067 --> 00:11:48.502
America in winter...

00:11:50.981 --> 00:11:52.116
The cold journey.

00:11:54.971 --> 00:11:56.582
But you were even colder than that.

00:11:59.835 --> 00:12:04.607
You didn't want to see your son
who came to the theatre to see you.

00:12:05.676 --> 00:12:09.205
I'm sorry. I'm so sorry, Terry.

00:12:09.240 --> 00:12:12.047
After all, wandering off to America
was stupid of me.

00:12:12.915 --> 00:12:15.833
I ran after you immediately after the incident.

00:12:16.472 --> 00:12:17.791
I don't want your excuses.

00:12:18.168 --> 00:12:19.820
Go back. Go back!

00:12:19.855 --> 00:12:20.716
Stop that!

00:12:21.222 --> 00:12:22.135
Stop that.

00:12:23.796 --> 00:12:26.702
Terry, be more truthful to yourself.

00:12:27.054 --> 00:12:30.368
-I am trutful to myself.
-That's not true!

00:12:30.541 --> 00:12:33.980
You're showing off by chasing away your mother,
whom you love more than anyone else!

00:12:34.537 --> 00:12:36.993
"Mother", was it?
Don't make me laugh.

00:12:39.310 --> 00:12:40.638
Please take a look at this.

00:12:42.227 --> 00:12:43.687
That's...

00:12:44.711 --> 00:12:48.222
-Terry is studying drama.
-Don't say unnecessary things!

00:12:49.587 --> 00:12:55.363
Regardless of how he feels about you,
mother's blood is running through Terry's body.

00:12:57.291 --> 00:12:58.314
Terry...

00:12:58.680 --> 00:13:01.480
Candy, if you keep speaking like that...

00:13:01.771 --> 00:13:05.873
I... I have no father or mother.

00:13:06.781 --> 00:13:08.907
Not that I wanted them too much.

00:13:09.476 --> 00:13:11.808
That's right... does it matter if
one has parents or not.

00:13:11.842 --> 00:13:16.564
I've never felt lonely since I had many friends
and kind sisters who took care of me.

00:13:17.932 --> 00:13:19.767
But once I arrived to Scotland...

00:13:23.339 --> 00:13:25.366
You look tired...

00:13:27.256 --> 00:13:31.817
When I saw that family, I felt so jealous.

00:13:32.263 --> 00:13:38.143
It doesn't matter how good your teachers or friends are...
they can never replace a mother.

00:13:39.521 --> 00:13:42.095
I... I want a mother.

00:13:43.049 --> 00:13:46.112
Any mother would do!
I just want a mother!

00:13:48.718 --> 00:13:49.669
Candy!

00:14:03.470 --> 00:14:06.243
I was just a little younger than Mark...

00:14:06.444 --> 00:14:07.657
...when it happened in the port - -

00:14:15.482 --> 00:14:16.474
Terry!

00:14:17.457 --> 00:14:18.518
Terry!

00:14:19.066 --> 00:14:20.664
Say, who is that woman?

00:14:20.856 --> 00:14:21.889
Some stranger.

00:14:21.890 --> 00:14:24.168
Terry! Don't take him away!

00:14:25.010 --> 00:14:28.962
-But she's calling out my name.
-Terry! My Terry!

00:14:29.486 --> 00:14:31.036
Papa, is that woman...

00:14:31.037 --> 00:14:33.734
Terry! Don't take him away!

00:14:33.757 --> 00:14:34.778
Terry!

00:14:35.068 --> 00:14:36.220
Terry!

00:14:37.570 --> 00:14:38.544
Look out!

00:14:39.042 --> 00:14:41.376
Now, it's too cold on the deck.

00:14:41.492 --> 00:14:43.463
-Let's go to the cabin.
-But...

00:14:45.538 --> 00:14:47.454
Terry!

00:14:51.342 --> 00:14:53.277
Terry!

00:14:54.539 --> 00:14:56.284
So that was mama.

00:14:57.139 --> 00:14:58.786
The real one.

00:14:59.653 --> 00:15:00.947
Terry.

00:15:02.448 --> 00:15:04.044
Terry!

00:15:09.765 --> 00:15:11.520
Our books are exactly alike.

00:15:12.403 --> 00:15:13.302
Books?

00:15:14.273 --> 00:15:19.529
I wanted to underline all the important parts but...
you've already underlined everything for me.

00:15:20.331 --> 00:15:21.168
Terry...

00:15:32.341 --> 00:15:33.969
I wonder what is going on...

00:15:34.148 --> 00:15:35.818
With Terry and his mother.

00:15:38.890 --> 00:15:40.958
Candy, is something wrong?

00:15:45.972 --> 00:15:52.386
Candy, lately you haven't been spending your
free time with us... have we hurt you somehow?

00:15:52.596 --> 00:15:56.490
Not at all! From tomorrow, I'll spend
my free time with you again!

00:15:56.525 --> 00:15:57.632
I'm so glad!

00:15:57.898 --> 00:16:00.141
We're lonely without you!

00:16:00.331 --> 00:16:02.543
Won't you ride a boat with everybody?

00:16:02.749 --> 00:16:05.570
Annie, you've got a tan!

00:16:05.883 --> 00:16:07.760
Aww, what'll I do!

00:16:08.445 --> 00:16:11.295
-There is a good way to protect us against sun!
-Really?

00:16:12.365 --> 00:16:13.939
Something to keep the sun away!

00:16:19.492 --> 00:16:23.778
-Annie, you got sunburnt in the boat?
-Of course! Right, Patty?

00:16:25.608 --> 00:16:29.754
My, my!
What's this, an uniform matching' practice?

00:16:30.005 --> 00:16:32.792
-Terry!
-I'm afraid...

00:16:33.635 --> 00:16:35.911
Candy, I'd like to have a word with you.

00:16:36.846 --> 00:16:39.439
Annie, Patty, go on without me.

00:16:40.180 --> 00:16:42.532
-You'll be okay alone?
-I'll be with you in a moment!

00:16:45.056 --> 00:16:46.757
They think I'm a rabid dog.

00:16:47.250 --> 00:16:50.769
Can't blame them...
You're the worst punk in school!

00:16:55.903 --> 00:16:58.505
I see. I'm glad you made up with her.

00:16:59.858 --> 00:17:02.740
I must thank you. It was all because of you.

00:17:03.929 --> 00:17:04.978
When you say that...

00:17:05.784 --> 00:17:09.330
I felt as if I had somehow trapped her
inside my body.

00:17:10.061 --> 00:17:12.892
-So your body feels lighter now, Terry?
-Yeah.

00:17:14.245 --> 00:17:15.374
It's your turn now.

00:17:15.541 --> 00:17:16.478
My turn?

00:17:18.552 --> 00:17:20.567
I'm going to free you from your shell.

00:17:21.391 --> 00:17:22.785
Now, Candy!

00:17:24.816 --> 00:17:26.325
Let go of me, Terry!

00:17:31.649 --> 00:17:34.202
Where are you taking me, Terry?

00:17:40.067 --> 00:17:40.888
A horse?

00:17:41.545 --> 00:17:43.923
-Candy!
-No... I don't like horses!

00:17:44.998 --> 00:17:47.445
Horse riding remembers you of Anthony?

00:17:48.661 --> 00:17:49.554
No!

00:17:49.714 --> 00:17:51.117
You will ride it, Candy!

00:17:51.242 --> 00:17:54.141
No! Please! Don't do this, Terry!

00:17:54.379 --> 00:17:56.621
I don't want to ride!

00:17:59.253 --> 00:18:00.721
Now, let's go!

00:18:01.171 --> 00:18:02.650
Please, put me down!

00:18:03.472 --> 00:18:05.193
You'll fall if you keep struggling!

00:18:12.938 --> 00:18:14.137
The sound of hooves...

00:18:14.223 --> 00:18:15.406
...on that day...

00:18:50.885 --> 00:18:52.056
Look out!

00:19:07.299 --> 00:19:09.299
Anthony!

00:19:21.610 --> 00:19:22.889
Anthony!

00:19:22.890 --> 00:19:25.273
Say it out louder!
Cry out louder!

00:19:26.059 --> 00:19:28.783
Stop... I'm begging you!

00:19:28.960 --> 00:19:31.699
Cry Anthony's name again!
Cry out to him!

00:19:32.096 --> 00:19:33.427
Terry!

00:19:33.594 --> 00:19:37.922
If you're so afraid, cry out to Anthony!
Cry out to him anytime! Just call him!

00:19:49.375 --> 00:19:50.395
Stop... I'm begging you...

00:19:51.439 --> 00:19:54.451
What's the matter, Candy?
Won't you call out his name? Call him!

00:19:54.740 --> 00:19:55.751
Stop!

00:19:58.224 --> 00:20:02.729
Dead people won't return!
They can't come back! Forget him! Forget him!

00:20:17.714 --> 00:20:19.724
Wait, Anthony!

00:20:31.714 --> 00:20:34.576
Candy! Open your eyes and look!
Now!

00:20:36.766 --> 00:20:38.193
Take a good look around yourself!

00:20:38.825 --> 00:20:41.600
Don't turn back towards the past,
take a good look towards the future!

00:20:46.442 --> 00:20:51.600
Green land... dazzling sun...
grass, trees and flowers...

00:20:51.786 --> 00:20:53.342
...every single of them is overflowing with life.

00:20:53.420 --> 00:20:54.752
Anthony is dead.

00:20:55.602 --> 00:20:57.568
But the two of us are still alive.

00:20:58.940 --> 00:21:01.397
We're as alive as these trees, grass and flowers.

00:21:04.146 --> 00:21:08.306
The burden you're carrying in your heart - -
Leave it in this forest, Candy!

00:21:08.307 --> 00:21:10.518
While Candy was hearing Terry's words,

00:21:10.519 --> 00:21:17.695
...she felt as if sad memories in her heart were
being slowly taken away from her, into the distance.

00:21:17.855 --> 00:21:20.005
to be continued ...
